{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D8","page":1,"quote":"-0.007"},{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D9","page":1,"quote":"-0.020"},{"kind":"note","ref":"N6","page":1,"quote":"# FINISH: IZBP"}],"comment":"Dimensions D8 and D9 define a tolerance band of 0.013 mm (from -0.007 to -0.020) on the shaft, but note N6 and the title block specify an IZBP plating finish without any allowance for the plating thickness. The added coating will push the finished shaft out of its tight tolerance, preventing proper assembly with mating parts. The designer must either increase the pre-plate size limits to accommodate the IZBP thickness or add a note specifying the plating thickness to be allowed for."
  ,
  "recommended_correction":"Adjust the pre-plating dimensions so that after IZBP coating the shaft remains within the required functional tolerance, or explicitly state the plating thickness allowance in the notes."}]}
